hermes v0.22.5: every gateway shutdown broadcasts "⚠️ Gateway shutting
down — Your current task will be interrupted." to the home channel of
every served profile (one multiplexed gateway per OS user fans the notice
out through each profile's own bot, #118233), whether or not any session
is running. Where every deploy restarts all native agents, each user's
home chat gets the notice on every deploy (two deploys in one evening:
nine home-channel sends, all with active_at_start=0).

The per-session notice to chats with a running agent stays; those
sessions are marked resume_pending and auto-continue on the next boot.
A chat without a running agent loses nothing to a restart, so the
home-channel pass in GatewayShutdownMixin._notify_active_sessions_of_shutdown
(gateway/run_shutdown.py) goes. The drain marker's suppress_notification
flag only ever gated that pass and is now inert; _notice_allowed's
platform_cfg parameter (served-profile opt-out, home pass only) goes too.

Upstream status (v0.22.5): no knob suppresses only the broadcast.
gateway_restart_notification=false and display.suppress_warning_notifications
also silence the per-session interrupt notice; the drain marker's
suppress_notification only applies to a dashboard-requested drain.

The tests that pinned the broadcast become its negation: no session ->
nothing sent (restart and shutdown), an active session is pinged while the
home channel is not (also for the interim-marker and warning-policy
tests), and no served profile's home channel is pinged without a running
agent. All fail without this change.

